==English==

===Etymology===
First coined by [[w:Alfred Kinsey|Alfred Kinsey]] of the [[w:Kinsey Institute|Kinsey Institute]], and later employed by [[w:Masters and Johnson|Masters and Johnson]] and the 1970 [[w:U.S. Census|U.S. Census]] forms.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈməʊ.təʊz/}}

==={{initialism-old|en}}===
{{en-initialism}}

# member(s) of the opposite sex

====Usage notes====
* Sometimes used jokingly in the [[GLBT]] community as part of the greeting "Hello MOTOS!", a parody of a "Hello Moto!" advertising campaign run by [[w:Motorola|Motorola]].

